# ==============================================================================
# Hermes Agent + OpenClaw (Debian 13 trixie) — ACCEPTED RESIDUAL RISK (UNFIXABLE)
#
# Scope: patches/hermes-agent and patches/openclaw.
# Root cause: Debian Security Tracker reports no fixed version (Fixed Version: None)
# for packages these runtimes need and which we deliberately do NOT purge:
#   python3.13 / libpython3.13*  -> OpenClaw skills (skill-creator, model-usage) and Hermes venv
#   libexpat1                    -> python3 / xml consumers
#   ffmpeg + libav*/libsw*       -> Hermes TTS / audio transcription tools
#   docker-cli                   -> Hermes docker terminal backend
#   libxml2, libcjson1, xvfb, libx11*, libxi6, libfontenc1, libxrender1 -> Hermes browser/media stack
#   openssh-client, git          -> Hermes terminal/ssh backend, git tooling
#   openssl, libsqlite3-0        -> runtime TLS / storage
# Purging them breaks features, so risk is accepted until Debian ships fixes.
# RE-REVIEW: drop an entry as soon as Debian publishes a fixed version.
# ==============================================================================
